      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "A solution to the linear equation $3x-4y=2$ is the ordered pair $(-2,k).$ What is the value of $k?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $(-2,k)$ is a solution to the linear equation $3x-4y=2,$ the equation must turn into a true statement if we substitute $-2$ and $k$ for $x$ and $y.$ So, we replace $x$ with $-2$ and $y$ with $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-4y & =2 \\\\ 3(-2)-4(k) & =2 \\\\ -6-4k & =2 \\\\ -4k & =8 \\\\ k & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
